<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21339] socklnd: a failed connect on one local NI closes the conns of the other local NIs</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21339</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Problem"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Problem&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A node has two or more local NIs on one tcp net. When a connect on one NI fails, socklnd also closes the conns of the healthy NIs to the same peer NID. The healthy NIs then reconnect. During a long failure of one NI, this close occurs again and again.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Environment"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Environment&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;master, 2.17.62.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;A client with 2 local NIs, &lt;tt&gt;tcp(eth0,mv0)&lt;/tt&gt;. A server with 1 NID.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Reproduction"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Reproduction&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Configure the client with 2 local NIs on one tcp net.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Start I/O from the client to an OST.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Drop all traffic on one client NI for 180 s.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Count the conns that the healthy NI makes to the server (&lt;tt&gt;New conn&lt;/tt&gt; lines in the debug log with &lt;tt&gt;+net&lt;/tt&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Analysis"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Analysis&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;ksocknal_peer_failed()&lt;/tt&gt; calls &lt;tt&gt;lnet_notify()&lt;/tt&gt; when the ksock peer of the failed NI has no conns. &lt;tt&gt;lnet_notify()&lt;/tt&gt; marks the peer NI down and calls &lt;tt&gt;ksocknal_notify_gw_down()&lt;/tt&gt; with the peer NID only. That callback closes the conns of every local NI to that NID. Each message that LNet receives from the peer marks the peer NI up again. So each later failed connect on the bad NI closes the healthy conns again.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17855" title="Router peer health feature is not working correctly" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-17855"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-17855&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (&lt;tt&gt;2a0127d5fba5&lt;/tt&gt;) added the down mark on each new report and the up mark on each received message. Together these give the repeated close.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Results on VMs, one dd stream, one NI dropped for 180 s:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class='table-wrap'&gt;
&lt;table class='confluenceTable'&gt;&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th class='confluenceTh'&gt;Build&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th class='confluenceTh'&gt;Healthy NI reconnects in the drop&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th class='confluenceTh'&gt;Down reports per drop&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;unpatched&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;63-73 (7 drops)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;7-9&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;patched&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;0 (9 drops)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class='confluenceTd'&gt;7-9&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;


&lt;p&gt;The lnet module parameter &lt;tt&gt;auto_down=0&lt;/tt&gt; stops the close. It also stops the down reports, which routers use.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Proposedfix"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Proposed fix&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Remove the close from &lt;tt&gt;ksocknal_notify_gw_down()&lt;/tt&gt;. The ksock peer that reports has no conns, so each other conn fails on its own error or timeout. The down report still reaches LNet. Add sanity-lnet test_551. It needs 2 interfaces.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
